WARZONE MOBILE OFFLINE – GODOT WEB PORT

An experimental Godot Engine port of my offline Warzone Mobile project. Built using locally extracted game assets, this version is adapted to run directly in a modern web browser.

The goal of this project is to preserve and explore the game's maps, modes, and core gameplay in a standalone environment—completely independent of the original online servers. The current build focuses on local gameplay, offline bot support, and smooth browser compatibility.

FEATURES
• Browser-Ready: Playable directly in a modern web browser
• Powered by Godot: Built with Godot Engine
• Original Assets: Uses locally extracted assets from the original game
• 100% Offline: Local gameplay with no server connection required
• Bot Support: Includes functional offline bots

CONTROLS & KEYBINDS
[V] Toggle third-person view
[K] Toggle flight mode
[M] Open minimap
[²] Open developer console

PROJECT STATUS
This project is still under development. Some maps, textures, menus, shaders, audio, and gameplay systems may be incomplete or behave differently from the original mobile version. Performance depends on your browser, operating system, and graphics hardware.

